<figure class="upgrade-paths" aria-labelledby="upgrade-paths-title">
  <figcaption id="upgrade-paths-title"><span>Figure 1</span><strong>Where the work falls</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="path-head"><span></span><span>Before the write pause</span><span>Inside the write pause</span></div>
  <div class="path"><p class="method">pg_upgrade</p><div><span class="phase-label">Before the write pause</span>Install, check and rehearse a separate copy</div><div class="paused"><span class="phase-label">Inside the write pause</span>Stop → transfer files → follow-up work → accept</div></div>
  <div class="path"><p class="method">Dump and restore</p><div><span class="phase-label">Before the write pause</span>Prepare target software; rehearse reconstruction</div><div class="paused"><span class="phase-label">Inside the write pause</span>Close source writes → dump final state → restore → accept</div></div>
  <div class="path"><p class="method">Logical replication</p><div><span class="phase-label">Before the write pause</span>Prepare schema → copy tables → follow changes</div><div class="paused"><span class="phase-label">Inside the write pause</span>Close source writes → apply final changes → complete service → accept</div></div>
  <p class="path-caption">A work map, not a time scale. Every route includes draining writers and moving callers. The logical route moves the bulk copy earlier; it adds a stream whose coverage and final applied state must be established.</p>
</figure>
